WEBVTT

00:07.760 --> 00:10.760
Darn it! There was nothing I could do!

00:10.760 --> 00:13.020
Am I not good enough?!

00:14.820 --> 00:16.990
You're not giving up, are you?!

00:18.890 --> 00:20.360
That voice!

00:20.580 --> 00:24.870
I don't recall raising anyone to 
get discouraged after losing!

00:25.240 --> 00:26.880
N-No way!

00:27.230 --> 00:29.590
No, it can't be!

00:29.590 --> 00:31.750
I saw it happen with my own eyes!

00:32.800 --> 00:37.820
We've been apart for a while, but my 
heart's been by your side all the time!

00:37.820 --> 00:39.640
My favorite student!

00:41.140 --> 00:43.150
Master!

00:43.350 --> 00:45.010
Now, let's go!

00:45.010 --> 00:47.630
Your fight has only just begun!

00:47.630 --> 00:48.820
You got it!

00:50.140 --> 00:51.880
Master!

00:54.150 --> 00:59.160
Master of the Lion's Fist

00:56.080 --> 00:58.610
It's so good!

01:05.020 --> 01:06.550
Are you all right?

01:06.790 --> 01:08.640
I am.

01:08.640 --> 01:12.450
I was reading <i>Master of the Lion's Fist</i>
yesterday and it was so interesting,

01:12.950 --> 01:15.560
I ended up binging fifteen volumes of it.

01:15.550 --> 01:19.300
<b>Hiiragi
Apartments</b>

01:15.560 --> 01:18.320
Oh, you've already finished <i>Lion Fist?</i>

01:18.320 --> 01:19.310
Yes.

01:19.650 --> 01:23.290
That one <i>is</i> good. Can't say I blame you.

01:23.290 --> 01:27.270
When the master died in 
volume one, it was a big shock.

01:26.770 --> 01:28.430
Master!

01:27.270 --> 01:32.050
I really sympathized with the protagonist, 
but then the master reappears in volume eight!

01:32.050 --> 01:35.820
I couldn't stop myself from 
restarting at volume one!

01:34.610 --> 01:36.820
<b>Master of the Lion's Fist
By Beefcake</b>

01:34.610 --> 01:36.820
<b>The hit series running in <i>Weekly Toys</i></b>

01:35.110 --> 01:36.820
<b>2nd anime season
coming soon!</b>

01:36.810 --> 01:42.030
That intense bond between the master 
and the protagonist is really great.

01:42.030 --> 01:44.730
Yes! No matter how far apart they get,

01:44.730 --> 01:47.900
they're sure to meet again as long 
as they keep caring for one another!

01:48.240 --> 01:51.090
It gave me such inspiration and courage.

01:51.640 --> 01:52.870
Agreed.

01:53.090 --> 01:58.840
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

01:53.400 --> 01:57.740
So, let's start figuring out 
how distance works for us.

01:57.740 --> 01:58.840
Ah, yes.

01:58.840 --> 02:03.340
It looks like retribution hits 
me if I get too far from you,

02:03.630 --> 02:07.860
so let's use today to figure out 
precisely how far apart is still safe.

02:08.200 --> 02:11.430
Yes, let's test this together!

02:22.200 --> 02:29.500
Looks like it started before I knew it

02:30.250 --> 02:35.300
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

02:37.210 --> 02:45.260
The usual townscape lends 
charm to the two of us

02:45.260 --> 02:50.770
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

02:54.520 --> 02:56.610
Suddenly buying flowers

02:56.610 --> 02:58.610
Standing around in the kitchen

02:58.610 --> 03:01.820
Sending a photo, because 
the setting sun is pretty

03:01.820 --> 03:06.370
Trying to spend as much 
time with you as I can

03:06.370 --> 03:09.370
This is all new for me

03:11.250 --> 03:16.920
I hope tomorrow is like today

03:17.250 --> 03:23.470
I've never felt this way before

03:23.470 --> 03:29.060
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

03:29.730 --> 03:34.980
But it's fine if we stay home

03:36.230 --> 03:39.440
I can't wait to see you

03:41.990 --> 03:46.990
<b>Episode 3</b>

03:41.990 --> 03:46.990
<b>Drama Bomb with the Princess</b>

03:47.530 --> 03:50.820
I got a fever before when 
we were two stations apart,

03:50.820 --> 03:53.750
so let's gauge things from 
here to that station.

03:53.750 --> 03:56.320
Okay. I'll be back, then.

04:07.040 --> 04:09.080
I wonder if she's on the train by now.

04:09.650 --> 04:11.280
At the moment, I'm fine—

04:17.110 --> 04:19.770
Did something happen?

04:19.770 --> 04:22.770
The packed train made me too uncomfortable.

04:31.270 --> 04:34.660
Looks like your mental state
 affects how I feel, too.

04:35.240 --> 04:36.680
I'm sorry.

04:37.150 --> 04:38.620
Oh, don't worry!

04:38.620 --> 04:41.440
After five attempts without any real trouble,

04:41.440 --> 04:44.050
we know we're fine if we're 
just one station apart.

04:46.360 --> 04:49.470
Shall we check on the other thing, now?

04:49.470 --> 04:51.550
Yes, you mean "contact."

04:51.770 --> 04:55.690
Last time, I was surprised 
when you yanked on my arm.

04:56.070 --> 04:57.100
Let's go.

04:57.100 --> 04:58.070
Ow!

04:59.160 --> 05:00.560
I'm sorry.

05:00.560 --> 05:01.400
It's okay.

05:01.400 --> 05:04.190
When it comes to things 
I wouldn't want people to do...

05:04.190 --> 05:08.580
Let's see what I can find in 
<i>Master of the Lion's Fist</i>.

05:08.580 --> 05:10.570
<i>You're getting ideas from </i>that?<i></i>

05:10.900 --> 05:14.450
This background character's 
behavior isn't nice.

05:14.450 --> 05:18.710
Of course we can rule out 
violence! Please switch genres!

05:18.710 --> 05:25.230
Then we'll use my favorite from the '00s, 
that huge shojo manga hit: <i>Prom!</i>

05:25.740 --> 05:26.780
Guess who.

05:25.970 --> 05:27.580
Guess who.

05:26.780 --> 05:27.710
Eek!

05:26.840 --> 05:34.480
<b>Eek!</b>

05:27.710 --> 05:31.700
The prank of sneaking up behind 
someone and touching their face.

05:32.860 --> 05:34.470
The way you say it...

05:35.070 --> 05:37.350
But, we <i>could</i> do this one.

05:38.320 --> 05:39.360
Well, then...

05:39.730 --> 05:40.760
Go ahead.

05:43.870 --> 05:46.870
<i>Calm down, this is an </i>experiment!<i></i>

05:48.420 --> 05:51.820
P-Pardon me!

05:53.890 --> 05:57.620
<i>Her head's so small! And her hair so silky!</i>

06:00.080 --> 06:02.620
N-Nothing much happens.

06:02.620 --> 06:04.400
I see.

06:05.730 --> 06:07.290
Why are you sweating?

06:07.290 --> 06:10.510
It's because I'm nervous. I think.

06:10.810 --> 06:12.330
That makes sense.

06:13.740 --> 06:15.020
Things like this are bad.

06:16.000 --> 06:17.280
That, huh?

06:17.280 --> 06:18.650
And please say the line!

06:18.650 --> 06:19.510
Right.

06:22.840 --> 06:25.010
W-Want to have some fun?

06:25.820 --> 06:28.890
<i>Silky! Smooth!</i>

06:32.310 --> 06:34.860
P-Please don't laugh!

06:34.860 --> 06:36.290
I'm sorry.

06:36.290 --> 06:39.960
It's just so amusing to me 
when it's pre-arranged.

06:40.850 --> 06:45.190
Let's continue. This has 
been on my mind, too.

06:50.430 --> 06:53.310
When someone else's face gets this close,

06:53.310 --> 06:56.010
wouldn't I react strongly against 
it even if it's pre-planned?

06:56.010 --> 07:00.180
Well, it <i>would</i> be intense to have 
this actually done to you!

07:00.890 --> 07:02.570
It's an experiment!

07:03.010 --> 07:05.180
<i>She's enjoying this, isn't she?</i>

07:07.660 --> 07:08.890
Go ahead.

07:08.890 --> 07:10.080
All right.

07:10.300 --> 07:13.190
H-Here goes!

07:13.720 --> 07:14.690
Okay.

07:25.450 --> 07:27.800
Ichiro, your phone was ringing!

07:39.260 --> 07:40.850
Making out here at home?

07:40.850 --> 07:42.240
Think of the children!

07:42.240 --> 07:43.440
That's not it!

07:43.440 --> 07:45.030
This is, um...

07:46.060 --> 07:50.740
Machi-san, this isn't making out.
 It's an experiment.

07:51.310 --> 07:52.500
An experiment?

07:53.250 --> 07:55.970
I was having Kuga-san help me.

07:56.420 --> 07:58.930
Thank you for going along with it.

07:58.930 --> 08:00.730
Oh, sure...

08:01.170 --> 08:02.690
Well, whatever.

08:02.690 --> 08:04.610
I did tell you about the phone!

08:07.210 --> 08:08.830
Are you all right?

08:08.830 --> 08:10.830
Yeah, sorry.

08:12.370 --> 08:13.760
What's the matter?

08:14.290 --> 08:17.070
I went beyond the peak of embarrassment.

08:20.600 --> 08:25.030
How about we stop for now
 and get back to work?

08:25.030 --> 08:26.390
Sure.

08:26.390 --> 08:31.290
As we explore like this, I hope you 
think of more things you'd like to do.

08:32.640 --> 08:34.660
Things I'd like to do...

08:34.660 --> 08:37.030
There are so many, it's hard 
to keep them straight.

08:37.030 --> 08:40.120
When think of them, why not 
start by writing them down?

08:40.120 --> 08:41.530
It might help sort out your feelings.

08:47.060 --> 08:48.620
<i>It's Morikuni-san.</i>

08:48.620 --> 08:51.550
<i>Maybe it's about the plot and color 
rough sketches I sent this morning.</i>

08:51.940 --> 08:53.660
Hello, Kuga speaking.

08:53.660 --> 08:57.560
<i>Kuga-kun, good work. 
Those sketches were great.</i>

08:57.760 --> 08:59.320
Thank you.

08:59.320 --> 09:04.180
<i>I personally like A, but B would 
work well in terms of composition.</i>

09:04.180 --> 09:06.730
Then I'll use the expressions from A.

09:06.730 --> 09:09.160
<i>Yes, please do.</i>

09:09.160 --> 09:11.910
<i>I've got a little something to discuss.</i>

09:11.910 --> 09:12.770
Yes?

09:16.100 --> 09:17.820
Let's see...

09:18.100 --> 09:21.030
Practicing with digital 
manuscripts on a computer.

09:21.030 --> 09:23.470
And looking into how that's done.

09:23.470 --> 09:25.770
Working digitally sounds like fun.

09:27.500 --> 09:32.200
If we can be one station apart, maybe I can
 get another assistant gig in the neighborhood.

09:32.740 --> 09:35.520
And it sure was fun shopping yesterday.

09:39.640 --> 09:42.600
Alice and the
 Knight of Thorns

09:40.400 --> 09:42.610
Reconsider upcoming developments?

09:42.810 --> 09:48.150
Yeah. Your art's been on fire 
lately with all the combat scenes,

09:48.150 --> 09:53.610
but a lot of people are musing that it'd be 
good to also focus on the primary love story.

09:54.020 --> 09:57.600
After all, emotion is important!

09:57.600 --> 09:59.600
I-I'll think about it.

09:59.600 --> 10:01.260
<i>Yeah, please do.</i>

10:01.610 --> 10:04.330
<i>Once you redo the plot, let's go over it.</i>

10:06.370 --> 10:10.220
<i>That means it's no good the way it is.</i>

10:19.380 --> 10:22.880
Uh oh, Ichiro's doing chores to avoid work!

10:23.230 --> 10:24.870
A-Are you okay?

10:26.390 --> 10:28.370
Want to touch Fumio's cheeks?

10:29.240 --> 10:30.770
Cheeks, huh?

10:34.550 --> 10:35.550
Squishy.

10:35.550 --> 10:37.140
Squish, squish.

10:38.500 --> 10:39.890
<i>This is serious.</i>

10:42.140 --> 10:43.900
Finished.

10:43.900 --> 10:46.650
It's my list of things to accomplish!

10:46.660 --> 10:50.170
Try lots of restaurants
Research metropolitan fashions
Write a news story
Have fun at an amusement park
Bungee jump
Stay up late
Make a friend
Go out with friends

10:46.960 --> 10:52.950
The latter half is largely just personal 
desires, but I'm a sensible grown-up.

10:53.770 --> 10:56.070
I will make these happen!

11:03.170 --> 11:05.400
Now what do I do?

11:05.400 --> 11:06.440
Kuga-san?

11:06.440 --> 11:07.460
Yes?

11:07.460 --> 11:10.020
Oh, are you cleaning?

11:10.040 --> 11:13.500
Well... sort of. What's up?

11:13.500 --> 11:16.360
I finished my list of things to accomplish!

11:17.730 --> 11:20.590
I thought I'd start with introducing 
myself to my new neighbors.

11:20.590 --> 11:22.990
And sure enough, you're first.

11:23.710 --> 11:27.000
Once again, thank you for all your help.

11:27.250 --> 11:30.870
This is just a little something. 
Feel free to choose one.

11:30.870 --> 11:32.830
Oh, thanks!

11:33.360 --> 11:36.250
Let's see, maybe I'll go with a towel.

11:36.250 --> 11:37.870
I'll cycle an old one into a rag.

11:38.640 --> 11:41.760
Don't tell me you do all the 
cleaning here by yourself?

11:41.760 --> 11:43.150
Oh, no.

11:43.150 --> 11:46.010
I do have a cleaning company come in.

11:46.010 --> 11:49.130
Oh, that's a relief.

11:49.130 --> 11:51.290
Are you going around to the other residents, too?

11:51.290 --> 11:53.570
Yes! See you when I'm done.

11:54.800 --> 11:57.280
They might not be here during the day!

12:03.650 --> 12:05.760
Looks like everyone is out.

12:06.240 --> 12:08.750
You might be able to get away 
with not worrying about it.

12:09.220 --> 12:12.030
It's common these days not to 
greet neighbors when people move.

12:12.030 --> 12:19.050
But I'm sure this is the way to treat 
those who live under the same roof as me.

12:19.320 --> 12:24.300
I can't speak for other places, but the 
people here don't go out of their way to mingle.

12:24.930 --> 12:28.180
O-Oh, is that how it is.

12:29.180 --> 12:33.690
Then how about writing letters, and leaving 
them with the gifts in the package boxes?

12:33.970 --> 12:35.400
Letters?

12:35.400 --> 12:38.680
I think I'd be happy to recieve a letter.

12:38.680 --> 12:41.330
That's a good idea! Way to go, Kuga-san!

12:41.870 --> 12:43.200
Don't mention it.

12:43.200 --> 12:47.690
Letters... That's exciting! 
I'll work hard to make them nice.

12:47.690 --> 12:48.640
Yeah!

12:49.190 --> 12:50.930
By all means, give it a go.

12:55.720 --> 12:57.100
I'm home.

12:57.990 --> 13:00.040
Chihiro-san, welcome back!

13:00.040 --> 13:01.410
Thank you!

13:01.410 --> 13:05.470
I apologize for not offering a 
proper introduction the other day.

13:05.750 --> 13:08.980
My name is Shiori Goshiki.

13:08.980 --> 13:12.470
Oh, no problem. I'm Chihiro Ibusuki!

13:12.470 --> 13:17.340
I have these as welcome gifts.
 Feel free to choose one if you like.

13:18.100 --> 13:19.690
Thank you!

13:19.690 --> 13:22.230
Let's see, I'll take the cleaner!

13:22.520 --> 13:24.870
Here, some cleaner and a letter.

13:25.520 --> 13:27.240
Thank you.

13:27.240 --> 13:29.740
Um, have you not gotten to the others?

13:29.740 --> 13:32.640
No, none of them were home.

13:32.640 --> 13:36.620
I wrote letters and was just about 
to leave them in their package boxes.

13:37.650 --> 13:40.240
That's like not getting to choose.

13:40.240 --> 13:42.620
Yes, it's unfortunate.

13:44.050 --> 13:47.970
<b>Room 205</b>

13:44.050 --> 13:47.970
Kuritsu-san (office worker)

13:44.100 --> 13:48.430
Kuritsu-san likes to eat. 
Soba noodles might be good for him.

13:48.430 --> 13:52.120
On the other hand, maybe something other 
than food is best for Honami-san.

13:48.550 --> 13:51.470
<b>Room 202</b>

13:48.550 --> 13:51.470
Honami-san (manicurist)

13:52.060 --> 13:54.480
<b>Room 103</b>

13:52.060 --> 13:54.480
Minakami-san (artist)

13:52.120 --> 13:55.050
Minakami-san would likely 
be happy with anything.

13:55.050 --> 14:00.030
Maki-san seems picky about the things 
he uses. So maybe not cleaner.

13:55.060 --> 13:59.730
<b>Room 206</b>

13:55.060 --> 13:59.730
Maki-san (restaurant worker)

14:00.030 --> 14:03.110
Oh! But that doesn't mean 
you have to go that route!

14:04.570 --> 14:07.030
We should be friends, if you'd like.

14:07.300 --> 14:09.030
A-All right!

14:09.990 --> 14:12.020
Oh, Chibi-chan's home.

14:12.280 --> 14:13.970
You met one of them on your own.

14:13.970 --> 14:14.990
I did!

14:14.990 --> 14:17.290
She gave me some cleaner and a letter.

14:17.290 --> 14:19.140
I have one for you too, Kuga-san.

14:19.140 --> 14:20.540
For me, too?

14:20.540 --> 14:21.910
Of course.

14:23.250 --> 14:25.410
Th-Thanks!

14:25.640 --> 14:27.310
No, thank <i>you</i>.

14:27.310 --> 14:30.410
This wasn't the same as typical 
new-neighbor greetings,

14:30.870 --> 14:33.420
but it was plenty of fun in its own way.

14:33.740 --> 14:35.480
I have you to thank.

14:44.940 --> 14:46.950
<i>She writes so politely.</i>

14:47.370 --> 14:49.990
<i>Her personality really comes through.</i>

14:51.940 --> 14:54.240
<i>"I wish for us to be friends"?</i>

14:54.240 --> 14:56.710
<i>"Don't hesitate to approach me"?</i>

14:56.990 --> 14:59.500
<i>That sounds a bit risky!</i>

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

14:57.200 --> 15:00.370
Is that safe?

15:00.740 --> 15:03.580
<i>Upholding public safety in 
the building is my job!</i>

15:05.510 --> 15:09.340
<i>That's important too, but right now,
 I've got a plot to write!</i>

15:25.210 --> 15:26.610
Good morning.

15:26.610 --> 15:28.870
Oh, good morning.

15:28.870 --> 15:30.760
Look at the whiteboard.

15:33.870 --> 15:38.870
Thank you.
--Maki

15:33.870 --> 15:38.870
Much appreciated! 
--103 Minakami

15:33.870 --> 15:38.870
They were delicious! 
--Kuri

15:33.870 --> 15:38.870
Goshiki-san, 
thank you for 
the cleaner! 
--Honami

15:46.670 --> 15:50.630
This is the start of a wonderful day!

15:51.630 --> 15:52.730
That's right!

15:53.890 --> 15:55.890
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

15:58.020 --> 16:01.020
It's no use! I don't have <i>any</i> ideas!

16:02.070 --> 16:04.860
After all, emotion is important!

16:09.490 --> 16:12.110
He seems very worried.

16:12.110 --> 16:16.360
Yeah. He said he had to redo the... plot?

16:18.460 --> 16:20.150
The plot.

16:20.150 --> 16:24.410
<i>Maybe it will cheer him up
 if I can help somehow.</i>

16:28.000 --> 16:29.020
She's here!

16:31.600 --> 16:33.800
Hi! Here I am.

16:33.800 --> 16:36.940
Welcome, Moka-nee! You weren't busy?

16:36.940 --> 16:39.850
I had just finished working and was baking.

16:39.850 --> 16:41.560
The usual apple pie.

16:41.560 --> 16:42.780
Yay!

16:42.780 --> 16:44.960
Are you a new resident?

16:44.960 --> 16:47.950
Yes. My name is Shiori Goshiki.

16:48.260 --> 16:50.940
I used to live here, too.

16:50.940 --> 16:53.190
My name's Momoka Morikuni.

16:54.120 --> 16:56.690
Moka-nee? What brings you here?

16:57.230 --> 16:59.690
I brought a pie. Let's have some tea.

17:07.380 --> 17:08.600
<i>It's good.</i>

17:09.590 --> 17:12.910
Moka-nee is Ichiro's childhood friend!

17:12.910 --> 17:17.430
And now she's married 
to his editor, Morikuni!

17:17.430 --> 17:19.970
We still call her "Moka-nee" out of habit.

17:20.380 --> 17:24.090
Moka-nee, Goshiki-san is 
working as my assistant.

17:24.090 --> 17:26.970
Oh, yeah? I draw manga, too!

17:26.970 --> 17:28.780
Oh, my! Really?

17:28.780 --> 17:30.890
She created <i>Master of the Lion's Fist</i>.

17:31.770 --> 17:33.620
She's Beefcake-sensei.

17:33.620 --> 17:34.990
Have you read it?

17:37.150 --> 17:40.870
I-I did read it! It was highly entertaining!

17:40.870 --> 17:42.240
Thanks.

17:42.240 --> 17:44.260
Oh, wow!

17:44.260 --> 17:49.400
Uh, I really like the master, 
and I ended up crying at that one part!

17:49.400 --> 17:53.750
I-I know! Could I ask you for an autograph?!

17:53.750 --> 17:54.840
Sure thing.

17:54.840 --> 17:57.170
Wow! Wow!

17:57.170 --> 17:59.260
Good for you, Goshiki-san.

17:59.570 --> 18:01.770
What kind of manga are you drawing?

18:01.770 --> 18:04.770
<i>Oh, yeah. I haven't heard, either.</i>

18:04.770 --> 18:10.060
I-I've started out with copying and 
studying art. I have yet to write a story.

18:10.760 --> 18:15.530
She said it's only been a year since 
she started reading manga or drawing.

18:15.920 --> 18:19.400
Is that so! Then you still 
have so much potential.

18:19.790 --> 18:21.560
I envy that. Good luck!

18:21.560 --> 18:24.780
A-Are you taking on new assistants?

18:25.610 --> 18:28.570
Assistants? I have enough at the moment.

18:28.570 --> 18:30.790
But maybe you could help 
out as a guest sometimes.

18:30.790 --> 18:32.450
Are you good at working digitally?

18:32.980 --> 18:36.290
I don't have any experience with that yet.

18:36.290 --> 18:40.760
I see. Last year I got married 
and went full digital,

18:40.760 --> 18:43.450
so all my assistants ask to work from home.

18:43.450 --> 18:44.820
Oh, all right.

18:46.420 --> 18:48.400
I have a tablet I'm not using. You want it?

18:49.870 --> 18:52.620
It's old, but it might do for practice.

18:52.620 --> 18:54.810
Wh-Why would you do me such a favor?

18:54.810 --> 18:59.060
I love manga, and I want the 
world to be more full of it!

18:59.060 --> 19:00.680
Thank you!

19:00.680 --> 19:05.070
That's good. I don't know much about digital, 
so I wasn't sure what to do.

19:05.360 --> 19:08.570
Do you still feel bad about 
losing my data that one time?

19:09.050 --> 19:13.830
I keep telling you, I still had the line 
drawings, and it didn't make me late.

19:13.830 --> 19:17.750
Kuga-san, you used to be 
Beefcake-sensei's assistant?

19:17.750 --> 19:19.580
Yeah, just for a bit.

19:19.840 --> 19:23.840
It's Moka-nee who taught 
him all about manga!

19:24.630 --> 19:25.980
That makes sense.

19:25.970 --> 19:27.980
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

19:28.500 --> 19:29.980
Thanks for everything.

19:29.980 --> 19:32.180
Did this help distract him?

19:32.180 --> 19:35.670
Machi messaged me that I should come over 
because her brother was down in the dumps.

19:35.670 --> 19:37.490
That's a secret!

19:37.490 --> 19:39.470
Yeah, I feel better.

19:39.470 --> 19:41.990
Cool, I'll drop by again sometime.

19:42.340 --> 19:43.980
See you later.

19:44.300 --> 19:48.490
Thank you so much for 
today, Beefcake-sensei.

19:48.740 --> 19:51.990
Don't mention it! And you don't 
have to use my pen name.

19:51.990 --> 19:55.470
Um, Moka-san... Momoka-san...

19:55.880 --> 19:57.020
Momo-Tea!

19:57.020 --> 19:58.700
You're sharp!

19:58.700 --> 20:03.900
Ichiro-kun was stressing over his shojo 
manga pen name, so I gave him my name.

